/* Factory design pattern is one of the creation design pattern use to provide object creation without exposing
    object creation logic to client.that provides a centralized way to create and return different subclass objects based on input.
     definition : It is used when we have super class with multiple sub classes and based user input or condition
     we need to return one of the subclass object.

     why factory design pattern
     1.> Loose coupling
     2.> Easy maintenance
     3.> centralized Object Creation
     4.> helps in achieving solid principles
     5.> Improves code reusability

     when to use factory design pattern
     1.> when creation logic of object is complex
     2.> when the client doesn't know which class object to create
     3.> When there are multiple subclasses of a super class

     Real-Time Example 📌
👉 Let's say we have a Payment System where we need to create different Payment Methods like:

Credit Card Payment
UPI Payment
Net Banking Payment
Instead of writing new CreditCardPayment(), new UpiPayment() every time —
We will use Factory Design Pattern 🔥.

     */